 Taliban are gonna really  regret what they did what do you say to  allies who look at the turmoil inside  the administration there have been 60  individuals in the Trump administration  of either resigned or been fired some of  them on the page here what do you say to  those allies who say hey listen this is  volatile it's uncertain we're looking  now at the fourth  National Security Adviser in three years  plus well here's how I'd say to allies  judges by what we do we reduced our  presence in Syria but we still have a  commitment to northeastern Syria to  protect the Kurds and make sure Iran  doesn't take over we got up at Orion  deal that I thought was a bad deal and  the president kept his word he's trying  to reduce our commitment in Afghanistan  and that makes sense to me we're paying  way too much money eighteen years later  and we can reduce our forces and be safe  here but we just can't pull out of the  place I'd say to our allies why don't  you help him more is was Iran a policy  difference between the president and  John Bolton because maybe the president  wants to meet with President Ronnie  maybe even at the UN General Assembly  I think Bolton looked at Trump to the  traditional foreign policy lens I've  abandoned that you know but condition  wisdom you don't talk to bad guys you  elevate kim jungim I don't care if  President Trump kim jungnam go on  vacation if that's what it takes to give  him up is give up the nuclear weapons  I'm okay with personal diploma this  unconditional I'm okay with talking to  the Iranians as long as we get a better  deal what would a better deal be they  can have nuclear power but they can  enrich or reprocess uranium that would  be a better deal so I'm not here to  lecture the president you beat me you  beat 16 other Republicans you beat  Hillary Clinton let's give your way a  try and I'm going to support them all  again but looking at North Korea as an  example as a blueprint how do you what  do you see out of those negotiations and  those two summits no well then where I  see better no nuclear missile testing no  bombs being exploded a personal  relationship that may lead to something  new and different everybody before Trump  how well did it work out so those who  want to criticize criticize the  president how well did you do in Iran  how well did you do in North Korea you  know I'm a pretty hawkish guy but after  18 years it's okay to reevaluate our  commitment in Afghanistan it makes  perfect sense to me but I'm just earning  the president don't ignore sounding  military advice you can reduce her  presence in Afghanistan but if you leave  Afghanistan al-qaeda and Isis are coming  after us  so did he fire him or did Bolton resign  I don't know and I don't think it really  matters at the end of the day I like  John Bolton he served honorably and this  president lost trust and faith in John  Bolton  and I think he's got some good choices  we talked about that you talked about  that today so we was on the  plate okay so general Kellogg is the  national security advisor to Mike Pence  the vice president he worked for general  McMaster Keith Killah yeah Keith Kellogg  he's a retired general competent capable  confident has the president's trust I  like him a lot Bryan hooks is a dynamic  young man working in the State  Department is part of the Iran team in  the State Department close to Pompeo  you've got Rick Waddell who worked for  McMaster that knows the ins and outs of  the National Security Council in the way  it meets the one thing that I think was  a knock on John Bolton as the inner  agency process kind of died on his watch  these are the three guys by the way  Keith Kellogg Brian Hook record oh yeah  so what I would say those are the three  names that the president mentioned to me  there are others on the list but what  are we looking for somebody that can  work with Pompeo can work with the  Department of Defense that can get the  interagency back stood back up this  doesn't require a Senate confirmation  vote this is just about trust with the  president right it's about understanding  the president trying to enact his will  but tell him the truth and here's the  truth and here's how I get along with  him this president you're right to want  to reduce our committment Afghanistan  reduced the cost and maybe reduce the  troop levels but it'd be a big mistake  to do in Afghanistan what Obama did in  Iraq so I'm looking for national  security adviser who understands the  president can work with others give the  president good advice and behind closed  doors push back when he needs to I want  to ask you two more questions one is  there's an investigation now of Commerce  Secretary Wilbur Ross if he put his  finger on the scale and NOAA scientists  and what in the fallout of the Alabama  ordeal we dealt with last week what's  your thoughts of that not good give her  crap okay that's for the record yeah  thank you  next question I mean you can't careless  this whole thing is a bunch of garbage  the President did have a model where it  could hit Alabama if it went through  Florida this is the Trump world the guy  can't do anything with a guy getting  criticized by a bunch of people who just  hate his guts and I'm not playing that  game the story about the Russian asset  that was extract another example of what  I think is complete BS  trying to blame the president for  something that didn't happen you know  other networks aren't there you know  saying the president got a loan  co-signed by oligarchs when it comes to  Trump I'm very suspicious you-you-you  say it then you try to verify it later  you know the president is a handful he  makes his fair share of mistakes but  this story about the president damaging  our national security I think is  unverified and untrue you confident that  the funding of the government is going  to go without a bump it may be a bump  but it's going to happen because  failures not an option and both parties  need to convince the public we're not  completely crazy appear and we can do  our job last thing anything get done  before 2020 in earnest I think we may  have some breakthroughs on solving the  plastic in the oceans problem we may  have some breakthroughs on  infrastructure a smaller bill funding  the government would be a great step  forward giving the military what they  need on immigration you might have a  deal with the daca population if the  court rules that Obama's daca plan was  unconstitutional you might have some  breakthroughs on prescription drugs  lowering the cost of prescription drugs  there's actually bipartisanship there  senator we appreciate the time thank you

